        Fact("seasons", "space", "Earth's axial tilt is the main reason for its seasons.", "The tilt changes sunlight angle and daylight duration across the year. The two hemispheres experience opposite seasons.", "When the Northern Hemisphere tilts toward the Sun, it gets longer days while the Southern Hemisphere gets shorter ones.", "NASA Space Place — Seasons: https://spaceplace.nasa.gov/seasons/en/"),
        Fact("sound", "space", "Ordinary sound cannot travel through a vacuum.", "Sound is a mechanical disturbance passed through matter. A vacuum has no material medium to carry those pressure waves.", "Radio signals can cross space because electromagnetic waves do not need the same material medium.", "NASA — Imagine the Universe: https://imagine.gsfc.nasa.gov/"),
        Fact("octopus", "nature", "An octopus has three hearts.", "Two pump blood through the gills; the third circulates it through the rest of the body.", "The hearts divide the work of moving blood through the breathing organs and the body.", "Smithsonian Ocean — Octopuses: https://ocean.si.edu/ocean-life/invertebrates/octopuses"),
        Fact("coral", "nature", "Corals are animals, not plants.", "Many corals consist of colonies of small animals called polyps. Reef-building corals commonly host photosynthetic algae.", "The animal and its algae partner can look like one plant-like organism, but they are different living things.", "NOAA — Corals: https://oceanservice.noaa.gov/facts/coral.html"),
