        Fact("bats", "nature", "Bats are mammals capable of sustained powered flight.", "Their wings are formed from skin stretched over elongated fingers. Gliding mammals rely on a different kind of movement.", "Gliding loses height while moving forward; powered flight can actively generate lift and climb.", "Smithsonian — Bat facts: https://www.si.edu/spotlight/bats"),
